2026-08-30 (relaunch #17) **THE 'OBJECT-STATE MODEL' IS NOT THE CAPABILITY — REFUTED DIRECTLY ON THE EMITTED .mlw, in minutes, and REPLACED with the right one.** The obvious fix for the frame honesty gap (and for the `_desugar_for` decline) reads "relate `setattr` to the `get_<attr>` projectors with a global attribute store". THREE shapes were tried against `why3 prove --type-only` (seconds each; the last kept at scratchpad/w2/attr_store_spike.mlw): (a) `val _attr_store : ref (map (int,int) int)` -> **"makes a ghost modification in the non-ghost variable"** — `map.Map` is a LOGIC type, so a program ref holding one is inherently GHOST, and ghost attribute values cannot flow into the non-ghost computation the emitted bodies actually do with them; (b) the same with a concrete `ref (Const.const 0)` — identical error, identical reason; (c) an `array int` store (a PROGRAM value) with `let function get_<attr> x = _attr_store[_attr_slot x k]` -> **"This function depends on external variables, it cannot be used as pure"**. THE TWO HORNS ARE EXCLUSIVE AND EXHAUSTIVE: either `get_<attr>` stays PURE and usable in `ensures` (the status quo — so `setattr` must be a no-op and the frame claim overstates), or the store is real and `get_<attr>` becomes state-dependent and therefore ILLEGAL IN ANY CONTRACT CLAUSE. THE REAL CAPABILITY IS TO MODEL THESE AST NODES AS RECORDS instead of opaque ints — exactly the machinery the emitter ALREADY has and already uses for `py_with_node`/`py_match_node`/`py_ghost_node` in the Module5 handler family, where `node.<attr>` is a native mutable field and the frame is a native `writes { node.<field> }`. That closes the gap BY CONSTRUCTION: no store, no ghostness, no loss of spec usability. AND THE COST IS FAVOURABLE: the corpus uses `setattr` in **ZERO of 814** files and declares exactly **ONE** `get_<attr>` projector, and only **TWO** contract clauses mirror-wide mention one — so this is very nearly CORPUS-INERT, a MIRROR-ONLY build. Recorded in the mirror at `_init_function_csl_fields`; emission byte-identical (comment-only, md5 checked).
2026-08-30 (relaunch #18) **THE CHEAP-WIN DRAIN IS NOW CENSUSED OVER THE COMPLETE SURFACE — 490 of 490 `\trusted` stubs with a live body, in ALL 44 mirror files, and there are ZERO faithful cheap wins.** The three previous censuses covered ~230 stubs in 22 files; this one covers every stub in every file, and it adds an AUTOMATED FAITHFULNESS SCORE so the verdict does not rest on eyeballing. New tool `scratchpad/w2/probe_all2.py`: port the LIVE body verbatim, re-emit with `--no-proof --keep-mlw`, and if L3-tc passes, EXTRACT THE EMITTED `let` BODY and count erasure markers (`str_hash_op`, `getattr_*`, `setattr_*`, argument-less oracles, `Array.make <n>` fresh locals, `if true then`, `: int` params). Cost: ~10 minutes for the whole surface (0.6 s per stub) — this is now the campaign's cheapest comprehensive oracle and should be re-run after EVERY capability lands. RESULT: 38 stubs pass L3-tc; every single one is a DECLINE on the emitted body. Six had a nominal score of 0 and each was read from the `.mlw`: `errors.PyCSLError.message` -> `(str_dunder_op ())`, a nullary oracle (`super().__str__()`, irreducible); `ir_resolve._inject_functions` -> `subscript_get !func_ir 1878939832` (hashed dict key), `insert_2 0 !func_ir` (the `ir_data["functions"].insert` receiver DROPPED) and `existing_add_1 (...)` whose result is DISCARDED while the guard reads `existing := set_comp 0` — the membership test is decoupled from the set it tests; `_Parser.error`/`unsupported` are trusted BY DESIGN; `sertop._sexp_tokens` is a GENERATOR; `Module3_Weaver._desugar_for` is the SOUNDNESS decline already recorded (L3-tc was never its wall — TERMINATION was). The remaining 32 carry `: int` params and `ref 0 in` locals — the pyval/opaque erasure — and 13 of them are the recorded `_Unparser` family. **TRAP (hh) NOW MEASURED AT 38 OF 38 OVER THE COMPLETE SURFACE.** LADDER RUNG 1 (cheap drain) IS CLOSED AT 492 MARKERS / 517 GREP, and closed with a REPEATABLE tool rather than a one-off reading. A NEW MEASUREMENT FALLS OUT OF IT: of the 38, roughly twenty are methods whose erasure is precisely `AST node -> int` (the whole `_Unparser` family plus the Weaver `visit_*`/`_attach_*` mutators), which is the FIRST quantification of the demand for ladder item 4, the record AST model.
