up still goes through the abstract val. The SCC-keyword post-process itself is byte-inert on its own (0 of 52 mirrors change without the marker). PROOF 1/2 GREEN: `src/self-annotate/src/pycsl.py` **731/731 Valid, SUCCESS**. `frontend/Module5_IREmitter` (1134 goals, the 20-member group) running.
2026-08-31 (relaunch #18) **INCREMENT 3 FULLY GATED: THE L2 DISPATCHER WALL IS BROKEN — `_py_expr_to_ir` IS CONCRETE, shadowed-selfcall sites 153 -> 125, and it costs NO AXIOM.** BOTH affected mirrors RE-PROVED: `frontend/Module5_IREmitter` **1198/1198 Valid, 0 non-Valid, SUCCESS** (1134 was the baseline, +64 goals, 0 emitted axioms — LEDGER STAYS 3) and `src/self-annotate/src/pycsl.py` **731/731 Valid, SUCCESS**. THE RECORDED FLOOR SAID THIS NEEDED A NEW AXIOM AND IT DID NOT. The record was right that the 20-member mutual recursion has no derivable common variant (the dispatch goes through the uninterpreted `val function pyx_view` over a type the preamble documents as NOT recursive, so `size_<T> (payload_of e) < size e` would have to be assumed) — but a variant is only ONE of Why3's two ways to accept a recursive definition. The other is `diverges`, which asserts NOTHING: it drops the function to PARTIAL correctness. THREE PARTS, each measured before the next was written. (1) The SCC GROUP KEYWORD post-process in `_emit_function`: nine bespoke group emitters hard-code their opening keyword as `let` and break the `let rec … with` chain FROM THE INSIDE (lesson (am) — a SYNTHESIZED body is a second producer of the group keyword); rewriting the keyword from the member's POSITION IN ITS SCC repairs all nine, and ON ITS OWN it is BYTE-INERT (0 of 52 mirrors change without the marker). (2) `#@ \diverges` belongs ONLY on the members that ACTUALLY RECURSE: Why3 REJECTS it on the other eleven with "this expression does not diverge", so a blanket application fails L3-tc — 9 of the 20. (3) THE CASCADE IS REAL AND BOUNDED, and it must be closed to a FIXPOINT: Why3 turns a call from a non-diverging caller into an undischargeable `Sub-goal termination`, so the first proof came back 1198 Valid / **50 Timeout** with termination sub-goals in `process_for/if/while` and nine `_py_stmt_*`. Computing the fixpoint STATICALLY over the emitted `.mlw` (any concrete block naming a diverging symbol) gave EXACTLY 12 more functions and then CLOSED — the propagation stops dead wherever a self-call still goes through an abstract `val`. 21 functions total. A FOURTH FINDING, and it is lesson (am) yet again: the dispatcher's own `#@ \diverges` was SILENTLY DROPPED because `_py_expr_to_ir` is emitted by the BESPOKE `_emit_pyx_dispatcher_bespoke`, which synthesizes its own contract block — the directive had to be added there too, and until it was, the dispatcher kept generating the 8 termination sub-goals it can never discharge. **THE HONESTY LEDGER OF THIS TRADE FAVOURS IT AND SHOULD BE READ CAREFULLY**: before this, the 19 handlers proved TOTAL correctness only because their recursive call went through the abstract `val self__py_expr_to_ir_1` — THE RECURSION HAD BEEN ERASED, so the termination claim was an artifact of the erasure and not a fact about the method. What is given up is a termination claim that was never established; what is bought is 28 call sites that now apply the PROVEN BODY instead of an oracle whose contract is `requires true / ensures true`. GATES: mirror sweep WITH L3-tc **2 of 52** changed, TC_FAIL 0; corpus byte-diff **0 of 814**; fidelity **2 DIVERGED** (baseline); mirror-check 3 drifted (baseline); untrusted-emitted **817/801/0/0**; shadowed-selfcalls **14 methods / 125 sites** (was 153), ratchet 14 HELD; emitted-vacuity --emit no NEW erasure, 8 known, 0 input-blind; doc-coherency GREEN; markers **492** / grep **517** unchanged. STILL WALLED: `_csl_to_ir` (92 sites) — its group fails L3-tc with `this expression produces an unlisted write effect`, a SECOND and DISTINCT wall (members of a `let rec … with` group must agree on their EFFECT SUMMARY), untouched by this increment.
